# From "Free Flow 12" (Wave IV - Adventure, CD2-3). Distinct from free.gws
# (a bare generic hold used at F12/F15/F21/F27): this one names the purpose
# explicitly and closes with thanks and closing any opened channels, rather
# than just ending. The tape's "beacon guidepost" audio cue has no equivalent
# directive in this format, so it's narrated in words instead.

@segment  free-flow-12
@title    Free Flow — Focus 12
@levels   F12
@duration ~5m

say Remember your purpose for this exercise.
pause 6
say Here in Focus 12, you're free. Free to send out questions and receive answers. Free to find whatever communication or information you're looking for.
pause 8
say Explore. I'll call you when this period is done.
hold 300
say Begin moving back now to where you started.
pause 5
say As you do, give thanks for anything you've received or communicated with.
pause 6
say And close down any channels you've opened.
pause 6
say You're back now, at your starting point. Calm, comfortable, and relaxed in Focus 12.
pause 6
